{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21879396",
      "title": "Diving Deeper Into Navigation Guards",
      "lectureOrder": 186,
      "videoOrder": 162,
      "sourceHash": "32a1465c61a5163d8a4b468554d8ed04c4cd195c2a8dad32724e14fc48d01d48",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.5,
          "end": 3.14,
          "en": "Now we don't just have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.14,
          "end": 5.65,
          "en": "this Global guard though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.65,
          "end": 8.773,
          "en": "This beforeEach function here will run",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.773,
          "end": 11.84,
          "en": "on every navigation action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.84,
          "end": 14.507,
          "en": "no matter which route is being used,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.507,
          "end": 18.17,
          "en": "no matter from which route we go to which other route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.17,
          "end": 20.127,
          "en": "this will always run.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.127,
          "end": 22.812,
          "en": "Sometimes this is what you need, sometimes it's not,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.812,
          "end": 26.645,
          "en": "sometimes you just wanna protect individual routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.645,
          "end": 28.07,
          "en": "You could do this, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.07,
          "end": 30.49,
          "en": "with a if check here, where you check your to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.49,
          "end": 31.711,
          "en": "and from route objects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 31.711,
          "end": 35.229,
          "en": "to also run different logic based on different routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.229,
          "end": 39.61,
          "en": "But you can also set up the beforeEach navigation guard",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.61,
          "end": 41.42,
          "en": "on single routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 41.42,
          "end": 43.97,
          "en": "For example, on users, let's say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.97,
          "end": 47.63,
          "en": "For that you simply go to your users route conflict,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.63,
          "end": 51.161,
          "en": "and here you can add beforeEnter, not beforeEach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.161,
          "end": 54.833,
          "en": "because now it technically is just one route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.833,
          "end": 57.496,
          "en": "BeforeEnter is a method here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.496,
          "end": 62.233,
          "en": "And just as beforeEach, it gets to, from and next.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.067,
          "end": 68.03999999999999,
          "en": "So here I console.log('users beforeEnter')",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.27,
          "end": 72.792,
          "en": "and maybe also console.log(to, from) is you want to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.792,
          "end": 75.157,
          "en": "and then call next to confirm it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.157,
          "end": 78.09,
          "en": "or do whatever you wanna do with next.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.09,
          "end": 80.239,
          "en": "Next works just as I explained it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.239,
          "end": 83.443,
          "en": "on the Global beforeEach navigation guard.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.416,
          "end": 88.31,
          "en": "Here I'm just confirming every navigation to users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.31,
          "end": 92.938,
          "en": "And now this will be called whenever we go to users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.938,
          "end": 95.803,
          "en": "So if I saved that and reload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.66,
          "end": 100.979,
          "en": "If I go to users, we see Global beforeEach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.979,
          "end": 102.93299999999999,
          "en": "because that still executes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.93299999999999,
          "end": 105.763,
          "en": "After all it executes for every navigation action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.763,
          "end": 108.066,
          "en": "But we also see users beforeEnter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.066,
          "end": 111.50999999999999,
          "en": "and then the output of to and from for this page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.50999999999999,
          "end": 113.663,
          "en": "To of course, is pointing at the users page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.663,
          "end": 116.613,
          "en": "because that beforeEnter hook was registered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116.613,
          "end": 118.293,
          "en": "for the users page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 119.82,
          "end": 121.414,
          "en": "Now, in case you don't wanna register",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 121.414,
          "end": 125.73,
          "en": "this on the route level or in your route conflict,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.73,
          "end": 127.191,
          "en": "you can also add a new hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 127.191,
          "end": 129.91,
          "en": "a new method inside of your component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129.91,
          "end": 132.84,
          "en": "Let's say in the users list component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 132.84,
          "end": 135.38,
          "en": "Here in your component conflict object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 135.38,
          "end": 138.497,
          "en": "you can add all those view lifecycle methods,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.497,
          "end": 142.553,
          "en": "like created or mounted and you can also add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.553,
          "end": 146.246,
          "en": "the beforeRouteEnter method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.246,
          "end": 148.697,
          "en": "If you use the view router, which we do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 148.697,
          "end": 151.915,
          "en": "this will be called before navigation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 151.915,
          "end": 155.108,
          "en": "to this component is confirmed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 155.108,
          "end": 160.108,
          "en": "And here again, you get to, from and next,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 160.27,
          "end": 162.4,
          "en": "and therefore we can do what he did before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 162.4,
          "end": 165.207,
          "en": "We can console.log('usersList Cmp beforeRouteEnter').",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 170.857,
          "end": 174.75900000000001,
          "en": "We can then console.log(to, from) of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 174.75900000000001,
          "end": 178.463,
          "en": "and we can call next or run any logic we wanna run",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 178.463,
          "end": 183.463,
          "en": "to confirm or deny navigation to next or redirect the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 185.685,
          "end": 188.86,
          "en": "And with that, if I go to Teams,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 188.86,
          "end": 191.534,
          "en": "reload, clear the console and go to users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 191.534,
          "end": 194.705,
          "en": "we see Global beforeEach and then to and from,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 194.705,
          "end": 197.473,
          "en": "users beforeEnter and then to and from,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 197.473,
          "end": 201.02,
          "en": "and then UsersList Cmp beforeRouteEnter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 201.02,
          "end": 201.853,
          "en": "And that's the order",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 201.853,
          "end": 204.603,
          "en": "in which these navigation guards execute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 204.603,
          "end": 209.056,
          "en": "Global is always first, then the route conflict level",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 209.056,
          "end": 211.223,
          "en": "and then the component level.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 213.1,
          "end": 217.036,
          "en": "All of these hooks run before the route is confirmed though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 217.036,
          "end": 220.22,
          "en": "which is why you can and have to call next",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 220.22,
          "end": 222.95,
          "en": "to confirm it manually or deny it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 222.95,
          "end": 225.373,
          "en": "or redirect the user somewhere else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 226.57,
          "end": 230.501,
          "en": "We've got two other guards related to loading a component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 230.501,
          "end": 233.277,
          "en": "One is the before route update guard,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 233.277,
          "end": 236.482,
          "en": "which you call directly inside of a component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 236.482,
          "end": 239.957,
          "en": "To be precise, inside of components which are reused,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 239.957,
          "end": 243.12,
          "en": "which in our case would be the team members component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 243.12,
          "end": 246.293,
          "en": "Here we got the parameter, the team ID parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 246.293,
          "end": 250.068,
          "en": "and it's absolutely possible that we are on the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 250.068,
          "end": 254.059,
          "en": "of one team and we load another team members page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 254.059,
          "end": 257.78,
          "en": "And then this team members page never leaves the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 257.78,
          "end": 260.431,
          "en": "and hence is reused, as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 260.431,
          "end": 264.629,
          "en": "In such cases, view router will call another nice method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 264.629,
          "end": 266.88,
          "en": "in the component conflict object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 266.88,
          "end": 269.178,
          "en": "Maybe here next to created,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 269.178,
          "end": 273.889,
          "en": "there you can add the beforeRouteUpdate method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 273.889,
          "end": 278.683,
          "en": "and view will call this method whenever this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 278.683,
          "end": 283.116,
          "en": "is about to be reused with new data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 283.116,
          "end": 284.802,
          "en": "because the route changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 284.802,
          "end": 288.317,
          "en": "So here we also get to, from and next,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 288.317,
          "end": 293.223,
          "en": "and then you can also deny or confirm the navigation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 293.223,
          "end": 295.994,
          "en": "just as you know it, just as I explained it before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 295.994,
          "end": 300.33,
          "en": "on the Global beforeEach hook, it's the same here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 300.33,
          "end": 301.927,
          "en": "And besides that of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 301.927,
          "end": 306.927,
          "en": "you can utilize to and from, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 308.281,
          "end": 313.281,
          "en": "to call loadTeamMembers based on the new team ID param,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 315.648,
          "end": 320.648,
          "en": "which you get on the, to be navigated to route object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 321.176,
          "end": 324.36,
          "en": "Now of course, we already have logic in place here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 324.36,
          "end": 327.105,
          "en": "to handle the changing team ID route parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 327.105,
          "end": 330.73199999999997,
          "en": "in this component, so we don't need beforeRouteUpdate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 330.73199999999997,
          "end": 333.558,
          "en": "for that, but using beforeRouteUpdate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 333.558,
          "end": 336.243,
          "en": "would be an alternative to watching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 336.243,
          "end": 338.44100000000003,
          "en": "the team ID prop, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 338.44100000000003,
          "end": 340.85,
          "en": "Though of course, with that hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 340.85,
          "end": 345.72,
          "en": "we again bind this component to be used with routing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 345.72,
          "end": 348.057,
          "en": "We use props instead of route params",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 348.057,
          "end": 350.65,
          "en": "to make this component more flexible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 350.65,
          "end": 352.01800000000003,
          "en": "When we use this alternative,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 352.01800000000003,
          "end": 354.22,
          "en": "we would make it less flexible,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 354.22,
          "end": 357.168,
          "en": "because this is only called if this component is loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 357.168,
          "end": 360.871,
          "en": "and reloaded through routing of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 360.871,
          "end": 363.941,
          "en": "But now this would be an alternative and with that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 363.941,
          "end": 366.867,
          "en": "we can console.log('TeamMembers Cmp beforeRouteUpdate') here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 373.294,
          "end": 377.53,
          "en": "and console.log(to, from) if you want to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 377.53,
          "end": 379.697,
          "en": "and then save everything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 379.697,
          "end": 381.98,
          "en": "And now if I go to a different team,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 381.98,
          "end": 385.639,
          "en": "we see beforeRouteUpdate runs and well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 385.639,
          "end": 388.671,
          "en": "then our logic in there runs, which we don't need here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 388.671,
          "end": 392.554,
          "en": "but I want to show you this hook of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 392.554,
          "end": 394.36,
          "en": "I'm going to comment this out though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 394.36,
          "end": 396.617,
          "en": "because we are already loading team members",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 396.617,
          "end": 400.51,
          "en": "when the team ID changes, we don't need to do this twice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 400.51,
          "end": 402.996,
          "en": "But that is another navigation guard",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 402.996,
          "end": 405.796,
          "en": "or another navigation hook you could also call it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 405.796,
          "end": 407.453,
          "en": "that is worth knowing.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
